{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-350404",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "For compatible matrices $A,$ $B,$ and $C,$ and scalar $\\alpha ,$ the Hadamard product has the following properties:\n\n- Commutativity:\n\n$$\nA⊙B=B⊙A\n$$\n\n- Associativity:\n\n$$\n(A⊙B)⊙C=A⊙(B⊙C)\n$$\n\n- Distributivity over Addition:\n\n$$\nA⊙(B+C)=A⊙B+A⊙C\n$$\n\n- Scalar Distributivity:\n\n$$\n\\alpha (A⊙B)=(\\alpha A)⊙B=A⊙(\\alpha B)\n$$\n\nIn this case, by the commutativity of the Hadamard product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{C}^{T}+B⊙A & ={C}^{T}+A⊙B \\\\  & ={[\\begin{aligned}4 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]}^{T}+[\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}9 & -2 \\\\ -4 & 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
  "html": "<div id=\"questionExplanation-350404\" class=\"questionExplanation\" style=\"display: block;\"><p>For compatible matrices <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"74\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D434 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2C\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"75\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D435 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2C\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> and <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"76\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D436 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2C\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> and scalar <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"77\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D6FC TEX-I\"></m